# The viewer usually needs NOTHING here.
#
# It falls back to same-origin /ws, which the Vite dev server proxies to the
# signaling port. That works locally AND through a tunnel, so one tunnel serves
# both the page and signaling and there is no URL to keep in sync.
#
# Only set this to point the viewer at a signaling server somewhere else:
# VITE_SIGNALING_URL=wss://your-signaling-host/ws

# TURN is NOT configured here. The viewer asks GET /api/v1/ice-servers for it,
# so the credentials live in services/api/.env.local and `pnpm turn` writes
# them there — no client ever ships one (ADR-0004).
#
# To force the relay path for a test, append ?relay=1 to the share or viewer
# URL. No rebuild needed, and it refuses to start rather than fail silently
# when the API hands back no TURN server.
